<div class="big_text">
<<nobr>>

    <div class="scene-container">

        <div class="story-box">

            <p>Morning light poured into the kitchen, bouncing off the tiled floor and the polished dining table. I walked in rubbing my eyes, still half asleep. Liz was already there, sitting casually with her phone in one hand and a cup of coffee in the other. The moment she saw me, a sharp smile formed on her lips. 
            </p>
            <div class="dialogue-row mc">
                <img @src="setup.ImagePath+'scenes/avatar/mc.png'" alt="MC" class="avatar">
                <div class="dialogue-box">
                    <div class="name"><<print $mc.name>>: </div>
                    <p> "Good morning." </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p>She looked up slowly, scanning me from head to toe like she was judging a failed experiment. 
            </p>
            <div class="dialogue-row up">
                <img @src="setup.ImagePath+'scenes/avatar/up.png'" alt="UP" class="avatar">
                <div class="dialogue-box">
                    <div class="name"><<print $up.name>>: </div>
                    <p> "Morning? For you maybe. Normal people have been awake for hours, you know." </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p>I pulled out a chair and sat down. Before I could reply, she leaned back, clearly enjoying herself. 
            </p>
            <div class="dialogue-row up">
                <img @src="setup.ImagePath+'scenes/avatar/up.png'" alt="UP" class="avatar">
                <div class="dialogue-box">
                    <div class="name"><<print $up.name>>: </div>
                    <p> "Honestly, you’re so lazy. Always late, always lost in your own little nerd world. I don’t even know how you survive without Mom." </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p>I clenched my jaw. Before I could fire back, Mom stepped in from the counter, placing plates on the table. 
            </p>
            <div class="dialogue-row character">
                <img @src="setup.ImagePath+'scenes/avatar/character.png'" alt="Character" class="avatar">
                <div class="dialogue-box">
                    <div class="name">Mom: </div>
                    <p> "Liz, that’s enough. Everyone has their own pace." </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p>Liz rolled her eyes but didn’t stop. 
            </p>
            <div class="dialogue-row up">
                <img @src="setup.ImagePath+'scenes/avatar/up.png'" alt="UP" class="avatar">
                <div class="dialogue-box">
                    <div class="name"><<print $up.name>>: </div>
                    <p> "I’m just saying the truth. He’s not exactly smart either. All books, no real-world sense." </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p>Mom sighed, giving her a warning look, but Liz clearly wasn’t done. The tension sat heavy in the air, thick and uncomfortable. This wasn’t just teasing anymore—it felt like a test. 
            </p>

Choice – How Do I Respond?

1️⃣ Fire Back – “Funny coming from someone who never stops talking.”
(Stand your ground and challenge Liz directly.)

2️⃣ Stay Calm – “You done? Because I’ve got things to do.”
(Keep control, refuse to give her the reaction she wants.)

3️⃣ Let Mom Handle It – Stay silent and look at Mom.
(Avoid escalation and let Mom shut her down.)

            <p>Liz watched me closely, waiting to see which way I’d go. Whatever I chose next would shape how this morning—and the rest of the day—would unfold. 
            </p>

        </div>
        
        <!-- EXAMPLE BUTTON -->
        <div class="enter-button" onclick="forwardTime(1)" data-passage="Home" style="width:25vw;">
            <p >Leave</p>
        </div>
    
    </div>

<</nobr>>
</div>